{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1337, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nGiven an array nums, you can perform the following operation any number of times:\n\nSelect the adjacent pair with the minimum sum in nums. If multiple such pairs exist, choose the leftmost one.\nReplace the pair with their sum.\n\nReturn the minimum number of operations needed to make the array non-decreasing.\nAn array is said to be non-decreasing if each element is greater than or equal to its previous element (if it exists).\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [5,2,3,1]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation:\n\nThe pair (3,1) has the minimum sum of 4. After replacement, nums = [5,2,4].\nThe pair (2,4) has the minimum sum of 6. After replacement, nums = [5,6].\n\nThe array nums became non-decreasing in two operations.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [1,2,2]\nOutput: 0\nExplanation:\nThe array nums is already sorted.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= nums.length <= 50\n-1000 <= nums[i] <= 1000\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def minimumPairRemoval(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1378, "char_start": 1349, "quote": "Input:\n[5, 2, 3, 1]\nOutput:\n2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1416, "char_start": 1390, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 2]\nOutput:\n0", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "844ce1e210fdc2f6ced158a851a5a94f9d0f8f17161ce4386495ee6c9515c7da", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "936c4ddfc299f38efaf7af526fc0cc901dd09840de41cabe8430754eedbd00f5", "seq": 2}
